Changes in this port
--------------------
The port keeps openTPU's architecture, instruction set, simulator, compiler and
host software, and re-targets the hardware to the Alveo U200:

  * rtl/boards/u200-vitis/, boards/u200-vitis/ — the Vitis RTL kernel and its
    shell integration (XDMA, four DDR4 MIG controllers, AXI4 memory path).
  * rtl/mem/otpu_axi_dram.sv — an AXI4 master in place of the LiteDRAM core.
  * opentpu/host/xrt.py, xrt_shim.cpp, libotpu_xrt.so — the XRT transport.
  * targets/u200.toml, targets/u200-vitis.toml, targets/u200-vitis-moe.toml —
    U200 build targets.
  * sim/verilator/tb_*axi*.sv, axi_mem_model.sv — AXI memory testbenches.
  * tools/power_*.tcl, power_monitor.py, area_report.py, diag_bridge.py — U200
    power, area and debug tooling.
  * docs/u200.md, U200_RUN_NOTES.md — the U200 board guide and bring-up notes.

Portions of the existing tree were modified to support that target; the
per-file notices described below identify them.


Per-file notices
----------------
In accordance with section 4(b) of the Apache License 2.0, files added or
modified by this port carry a short notice in a comment at the top of the file:

  "Modified for the XCU200 port (WingardAI, 2026) from openTPU, ..."
  "New in the XCU200 port (WingardAI, 2026) for openTPU, ..."

Files that already carried their own upstream copyright or license headers keep
those headers unchanged; the port's notice is added alongside them, never in
place of them. Two such cases are worth naming:

  * tools/litedram/*.py — derived from LiteDRAM, BSD-2-Clause, with the
    original copyright notices retained in their docstrings.
  * boards/bcu1525/constraints/*.xdc and boards/bcu1525/scripts/gen_pins.py —
    generated from AMD XilinxBoardStore pin data (Copyright 2023 Advanced Micro
    Devices, Inc., Apache License 2.0).

Generated files carry no notice of their own, because they are outputs of
checked-in generators and are marked "do not edit" at the top:

  * boards/bcu1525/constraints/bcu1525_pins.xdc (gen_pins.py)
  * rtl/boards/ypcb-00338/otpu_fpga_top_ld.sv

Data and vendor configuration files carry no notice either, because their
formats do not admit comments: *.json, *.jsonl, *.xci, *.xml, and the compiled
opentpu/host/libotpu_xrt.so. Their provenance is the port's and openTPU's, as
described here.


